.TH LEAKCHECK 1 "2026" "leakcheck 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
leakcheck \\- find memory bugs, leaked resources, weak source and malware in C and C++ programs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B leakcheck
.I mode
.RI [ options ]
.I target
.RI [ target-args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B leakcheck
has three independent modes that share one reporter, so the console, JSON,
SARIF and JUnit output and the exit status are the same from each.
.TP
.B dynamic
Runs the program with a tracking library loaded into it and reports what
actually happened: leaks, double frees, use after free, overflows, leaked
descriptors and processes, deadlocks, and what a trojan does to the machine.
The program is executed; run untrusted programs in a virtual machine.
.TP
.B static
Parses C and C++ sources and follows pointers, handles and locks through each
function, and reads the source for weaknesses such as format strings, command
injection, unbounded copies, hard-coded secrets and check-then-use races. There
is no compiler front end, so it runs anywhere in milliseconds and is tuned for
few false alarms rather than completeness.
.TP
.B scan
Reads files and folders for signs of malware without executing anything.
.TP
.B ai-features
Prints the numbers
.B scan --ai
reads from each Windows program. It exists for training the classifier.
.SH OPTIONS
Options go before the target. In dynamic mode everything after the program is
passed to it unchanged.
.TP
.BR \\-o ", " \\-\\-output " " \\fIfile\\fR
Write the report to \\fIfile\\fR instead of standard output; \\fB-\\fR explicitly
selects standard output. Structured dynamic reports require a real file so the
target's output cannot corrupt them.
.TP
.BR \\-f ", " \\-\\-format " " \\fIconsole|json|sarif|junit|html|markdown|csv|gitlab|sonarqube|patch\\fR
Output format. The default is \\fBconsole\\fR; \\fBsarif\\fR is SARIF 2.1.0 for
code-scanning services, \\fBjunit\\fR is for test reports, \\fBhtml\\fR is one self-contained page,
\\fBmarkdown\\fR (\\fBmd\\fR) is for pull-request summaries, \\fBcsv\\fR is for audit export,
\\fBgitlab\\fR is for GitLab Code Quality JSON, \\fBsonarqube\\fR is for SonarQube Generic Issue Import,
and \\fBpatch\\fR produces unified diff auto-fixes.
.TP
.BR \\-\\-diff\\-base " " \\fIref\\fR
Static mode: only report findings on lines modified relative to git \\fIref\\fR.
.TP
.B \\-\\-metrics ", " \\-\\-stats
Include codebase security metrics, issue density, and technical debt score in the report.
.TP
.BR \\-s ", " \\-\\-suppressions " " \\fIfile\\fR
Ignore findings matching rules written as \\fItype\\fR:\\fIpattern\\fR. A rule
may carry \\fBreason="..."\\fR and \\fBexpires=YYYY\\-MM\\-DD\\fR; an expired rule
is an error, and the file is checked before the target runs.
.TP
.B \\-\\-audit\\-suppressions
Print every rule with its reason and how long it has left, and fail if one has
expired.
.TP
.BR \\-\\-baseline " " \\fIwrite\\fR|\\fIcompare\\fR " " \\fIfile\\fR
Write the findings this tree has now, or fail only on findings that are not in
the baseline. Fingerprints survive reformatting and moved code.
.TP
.BR \\-\\-exclude " " \\fIglob\\fR
Do not read files that match. Repeatable. \\fI.leakcheckignore\\fR and the
config file can add more; the report says how many files they hid.
.TP
.BR \\-\\-min\\-severity " " \\fIerror|warning|note\\fR
The weakest finding that fails the gate. The default is \\fBwarning\\fR.
.TP
.BR \\-\\-error\\-exitcode " " \\fIn\\fR
Exit status when problems are found, 1 to 255. The default is 2.
.TP
.BR \\-\\-config " " \\fIfile\\fR ", " \\-\\-no\\-config
Use this file instead of the nearest \\fIleakcheck.toml\\fR, or ignore the config
and \\fI.leakcheckignore\\fR entirely.
.TP
.B \\-\\-print\\-config
Print the effective settings after the config file and the flags, and exit.
.TP
.B \\-\\-rule\\-list
Print every rule with its CWE, severity and whether it is on by default; with
\\fB\\-f json\\fR, for inventory tools.
.TP
.BR \\-\\-enable\\-rule " " \\fIid\\fR
Enable one rule, including one strict-only rule, without enabling all strict
checks. Repeatable. A command-line setting overrides the config file.
.TP
.BR \\-\\-disable\\-rule " " \\fIid\\fR
Remove one rule from every report format and from the exit-status calculation.
Repeatable. Rule IDs are listed by \\fB\\-\\-rule\\-list\\fR.
.TP
.BR \\-\\-changed\\-only " " \\fIref\\fR
Static mode: analyse only the files that differ from the git \\fIref\\fR.
.TP
.B \\-\\-no\\-cache
Static mode: do not read or write the incremental cache.
.TP
.B \\-\\-strict
Also report the rules that missed the false-alarm budget; they are off by
default.
.TP
.B \\-\\-malware
Also look for the 100 malware families, in files, in source and in what the
program does. Much slower; off by default.
.TP
.B \\-\\-ai
In scan mode, also ask the trained classifier about every Windows program.
Needs \\fImodel/pe\\-malware.ai\\fR.
.TP
.BR \\-\\-ai\\-model " " \\fIfile\\fR ", " \\-\\-ai\\-threshold " " \\fI0..1\\fR
Use another model, or another score above which a file counts as malware.
.TP
.BR \\-j ", " \\-\\-jobs " " \\fIn\\fR
Files read at the same time, for scan, static and ai-features. The default is
one per CPU; the report is identical for any number.
.TP
.BR \\-V ", " \\-\\-version
Print the version, the commit it was built from, the build type and the
classifier it would use.
.TP
.BR \\-h ", " \\-\\-help
Print the full option list, including the dynamic-mode options
(\\fB\\-\\-guard\\-every\\fR, \\fB\\-\\-quarantine\\-mb\\fR, \\fB\\-\\-stack\\-depth\\fR,
\\fB\\-\\-fast\\-unwind\\fR, \\fB\\-\\-abort\\-on\\-error\\fR, \\fB\\-\\-trace\\-children\\fR,
\\fB\\-\\-show\\-reachable\\fR, \\fB\\-\\-no\\-leak\\-check\\fR).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean. In dynamic mode the program's own status is returned instead, and
\\fB127\\fR when it could not be started.
.TP
.B 2
Something was found (change with \\fB\\-\\-error\\-exitcode\\fR).
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, or nothing could be analysed.
.TP
.B 3
The config, baseline or suppression file is wrong.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I leakcheck.toml
Settings found upwards from the target: format, jobs, excludes, suppression
files, rule policy and per-mode thresholds. Flags win over the file.
.TP
.I .leakcheckignore
Globs of files to leave unread, one per line. A later \\fB!\\fR pattern
re-includes files; \\fB\\e!\\fR and \\fB\\e#\\fR match literal leading markers.
.TP
.I .leakcheck-cache
Static mode's per-file cache, kept beside the analysed tree and keyed by file
content, parser version and flags. Remove it at any time.
.TP
.I model/pe\\-malware.ai
The shipped classifier, found next to the binary, next to the project root, or
under \\fIshare/leakcheck/model\\fR.
.TP
.I libleakcheck_preload.so
The runtime injected in dynamic mode. On Windows,
\\fIleakcheck_preload.dll\\fR. It must stay beside the \\fBleakcheck\\fR binary.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
leakcheck dynamic ./my_program arg1
leakcheck static src/ \\-f sarif \\-o leakcheck.sarif
leakcheck static . \\-\\-baseline compare .leakcheck-baseline
leakcheck scan ./downloads/
leakcheck scan \\-\\-ai ./downloads/ \\-f json \\-o scan.json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The full reference, the design notes, the rule pages and the model
description are installed under \\fIshare/doc/leakcheck\\fR and kept in the
source tree under \\fIdocs/\\fR.
